		"ui.back": "Back",
		"howto.day.title": "Day",
		"howto.day.text": "People live in the village, and vampires live among them. Vampires look like everyone else. You are a villager with a lantern.\n\nBy day everyone is on the square. Tap a villager: accuse them, invite them to spend the night together or ask where they're sleeping. A red eye over a head means the village suspects them.\n\nTap a job icon: water, firewood, lamps. The more supplies, the brighter the night. Vampires pretend to work or even spoil what's done. Sometimes a box appears on the square: whoever opens it first gets what's inside.",
		"howto.night.title": "Night",
		"howto.night.text": "In the evening the bell rings and everyone runs home. While it rings, tap a house. There are fewer shelters than people: whoever stays outside will hardly see the morning.\n\nBeing alone in a house is risky too. In the day, agree on who you'll sleep with and fix a cracked charm: the thing from the forest comes into a house with a broken one.",
		"howto.door.title": "The door",
		"howto.door.text": "Whoever reaches a house first decides who gets in.\n\nLet in a vampire and you won't see the morning. Let in nobody and you're alone. In the morning, check who slept where and who lied.\n\nSometimes the knocking comes in the voice of someone who is in another house or already dead. That's the Mimic: don't open.\n\nSome people have roles: Elder, Healer, Headman. Once a game you can ring the bell in the day and vote right away. Everything known about each villager is in the Diary.",
		"howto.title": "How to play · {a} of {b}",
