		"camp.a1c1.title": "The Knock",
		"camp.a1c1.desc": "Your first night in the village. Someone knocks, and you don't know the rules yet.",
		"camp.a1c1.beat1_title": "The Knock",
		"camp.a1c1.beat1": "The stove isn't even warm yet, and someone is already knocking.",
		"camp.a1c1.beat2_title": "The rules",
		"camp.a1c1.beat2": "You'll learn the rules as you go. First, decide whether to open.",
		"camp.a1c2.title": "Fog",
		"camp.a1c2.desc": "Two people arrive from the road. Fog rises from the river, and the vampire must be found before the third night.",
		"camp.a1c2.beat1_title": "Chapter 2. Fog",
		"camp.a1c2.beat1": "After the first night two people came from the road. They say doors in the next village no longer open.",
		"camp.a1c2.beat2_title": "Before the third night",
		"camp.a1c2.beat2": "By evening fog rises from the river. On such a night the bell is harder to hear. Find the vampire before it finds you.",
		"camp.a1c3.title": "Farewell",
		"camp.a1c3.desc": "The last nights in the village. There are two vampires now, and everyone has to leave for the mill together.",
		"camp.a1c3.beat1_title": "Chapter 3. Farewell",
		"camp.a1c3.beat1": "The headman has decided: if we survive these nights, we leave for the mill by the river. We can't stay here any longer.",
		"camp.a1c3.beat2_title": "Two",
		"camp.a1c3.beat2": "There are two vampires now. One of your own is no longer one of you, and only yesterday you shared bread.",
		"camp.act1.end_all": "Almost the whole village leaves for the mill. Only the charms stay behind in the empty houses.",
		"camp.act1.end_some": "Only a few leave for the mill. Nobody wants to look back.",
		"camp.act1.end_none": "You go to the mill without the people you came with. All that's left of the village is names.",
		"goal.people_win": "The people must hold out",
		"goal.survive": "Survive to the end",
		"goal.exile_upyr_by_3": "Drive out the vampire before the third night",
		"goal.no_wrong_exile": "Don't drive out a single human",
		"goal.admit_night1": "Open the door on the first night",
		"goal.inspect": "Inspect someone knocking at the door",
		"goal.keep_couple": "Keep the couple alive: both must survive",
		"mo.guest": "{who}, the newcomer",
		"mo.guest_reveal": "The secret of {who}",
		"guest.soldier.name": "Gideon",
		"guest.soldier.title": "Newcomer, {n}. A soldier without a regiment",
		"guest.soldier.story": "He came off the road in a greatcoat that doesn't fit. Says his regiment is camped across the river and will come for him soon. He sleeps sitting up, knife in hand.",
		"guest.soldier.clue1": "This morning at the well {who} was scrubbing something dark off his coat. He said it was clay.",
		"guest.soldier.clue2": "Inside {who}'s coat someone else's name is stitched. “Took it off a dead man,” he says, and explains nothing more.",
		"guest.soldier.reveal_h": "{who} deserted when his regiment was surrounded in the forest. He is not a vampire. He left his comrades behind and is afraid you'll leave him now.",
		"guest.soldier.reveal_u": "By the river where {who}'s regiment camped, empty greatcoats were found and not a single body. Bare footprints lead from them to the village. The same prints are by the doorstep where he sleeps.",
		"guest.widow.name": "Agatha",
		"guest.widow.title": "Widow, {n}. Came with a cart",
		"guest.widow.story": "She came on a cart covered with sacking. Says her son sleeps under it and mustn't be woken. In the evenings she sings to him.",
		"guest.widow.clue1": "At night {who} sang a lullaby by the cart. Those who came closer heard only silence in reply: nothing under the sacking moves.",
		"guest.widow.clue2": "{who} lets no one near the cart. Says her son is sick and the light hurts him. A neighbour's dog howls by the wheels.",
		"guest.widow.reveal_h": "Under the sacking lie a child's shirt and small boots. {who}'s son has been gone a year. She is not a vampire. She never managed to bury him.",
		"guest.widow.reveal_u": "Under the sacking there is nothing but straw with brown stains. “He went out for a walk,” {who} smiles. At night someone was eating quietly by the cart.",
		"guest.merchant.name": "Ephraim",
		"guest.merchant.title": "Merchant, {n}. Sells charms",
		"guest.merchant.story": "He carries charms of thistle and salt in a box. Sells them cheap and gives them free to the poor. Says the villages along the road are alive thanks to him.",
		"guest.merchant.clue1": "A charm bought from {who} cracked on the very first night. {who} shrugged: “Then you held it wrong.”",
		"guest.merchant.clue2": "In the villages {who} passed through, the doors no longer open. He tells you so himself and laughs.",
		"guest.merchant.reveal_h": "{who}'s charms are fake: salt mixed with chalk. He made money on your fear. But the blood on his hands isn't his: he spent half the night bandaging a wounded man by the river.",
		"guest.merchant.reveal_u": "At the bottom of {who}'s box they found thin, gnawed bones. He made his charms from what was left of his customers.",
